ith him in Lewiston.\n\nPolling is mixed: a late-September University of New Hampshire survey shows Dunlap up six, while earlier surveys were tied or slightly Republican. Expert ratings split between Lean R and Tossup, and prediction markets give LePage roughly a two-thirds chance. The race sits right on the edge between the two parties, with ranked-choice voting potentially decisive in a close finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4239, "margin": -1.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.38, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3812, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.377, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3179, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4062, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4214, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.437, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4556, "margin": -1.0}]}